11	// This file is the regression net for a dangling symbolic link on a DIRECTORY
12	// component of the registry path. With work/alias pointing at a directory that
13	// does not exist, reading work/alias/batches.json reaches no file the way the
14	// kernel resolves names — the missing target is not a missing registry file,
15	// and a ".." right after the link (work/alias/../batches.json) cannot step
16	// out of a directory that was never reached, so even an existing
17	// work/batches.json must not be read in its place. The rule under guard is
18	// that Load fails such a path at the read stage: a non-nil error quoting the
19	// path the caller passed verbatim and a nil registry, never the
20	// err == nil / existed == false signal of a first registration. The read
21	// creates nothing and changes nothing.
